# digital.sbb.ch – SBB Design Systems

> Official guidelines of SBB (Swiss Federal Railways) for digital products. SBB has several design systems: Lyne for the web, the mobile design system for native apps and the legacy Angular library Lean. Principles, foundations, accessibility and writing rules apply to all of them.

This file was generated on {{ buildTime }} and is rebuilt daily; if your copy is clearly older, it comes from a cache (yours or your fetch tool's), not from this server.

## Choose the design system first

Read the file for your platform before writing code. Check the project to decide:

- [Lyne (web)]({{ site }}/design-system/lyne/llms.txt): Websites and web applications, web components `@sbb-esta/lyne-elements` and the Angular wrapper `@sbb-esta/lyne-angular`. Use it if `package.json` contains one of these packages, or for any new web project.
- [Mobile (native apps)]({{ site }}/design-system/mobile/llms.txt): iOS, Android and Flutter apps. Use it if the project contains `pubspec.yaml` (Flutter), an `.xcodeproj` or `Package.swift` (SwiftUI) or `build.gradle.kts` with Jetpack Compose (Android).
- [Lean (legacy)]({{ site }}/design-system/lean/llms.txt): Only for existing applications that depend on `@sbb-esta/angular`. Not for new projects.

Do not mix design systems: Lyne components do not exist in native apps, and Lean components are not Lyne components even though both use the prefix `sbb-`.

## Markdown versions

- Pages are available as Markdown: `index.md` next to the HTML page (`{{ site }}/<lang>/…/index.md`), in English and German only (French and Italian pages have the same content; use the English or German page). The lists below link the English versions; German versions have the same path with `/de/` instead of `/en/`.
- Pages that only redirect (e.g. `/en/foundation/`, `/en/foundation/colors/`) have no Markdown version; use the sub pages listed below (e.g. `/en/foundation/colors/base-colors/index.md`).
- Servers answer `Accept: text/markdown` on a page URL (ending with `/`) with the Markdown version if one exists (`Vary: Accept`).
- [UI icon names]({{ site }}/icons-ui.json): All valid SBB UI icon names with sizes, category and keywords.
